// Customer relationships - one row per (user, operator) pair, created the
// first time a CONFIRMED booking links that user to that operator. Confirmed
// is the bar because confirmation is payment-gated, and without a successful
// payment there is no customer: a row is never minted from an empty ledger
// (see CustomerProvisioningService.recomputeAggregates). An existing row CAN
// fall to zero when its bookings are cancelled - that is history, not a
// phantom.
//
// Purpose: marks a USER-role account as a CUSTOMER of a tour operator and
// carries denormalized aggregates for the future operator-facing "Customers"
// page. The customer-facing dashboard never reads these snapshots - its
// totals come live from the bookings/payments ledger (GET /bookings/me/summary).
//
// Aggregates are recomputed-on-write (groupBy over the user's CONFIRMED
// bookings for the operator, then upsert) - idempotent and self-healing, no
// increment drift. totalSpendEur is the confirmed-booking EUR value snapshot;
// refunds do not adjust it (documented in technical-doc/customers/).

model Customer {
  id             String    @id @default(uuid())
  userId         String
  operatorId     String
  firstBookingAt DateTime?
  lastBookingAt  DateTime?
  bookingsCount  Int       @default(0)
  totalSpendEur  Decimal   @default(0) @db.Decimal(12, 2)
  createdAt      DateTime  @default(now())
  updatedAt      DateTime  @updatedAt

  user     User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  operator Operator @relation(fields: [operatorId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@unique([userId, operatorId])
  @@index([operatorId])
  @@map("customers")
}
